      "id": 1,
      "text": "Founded in 1818, Fredericktown ranks among the oldest communities west of the Mississippi.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.fredericktownmo.org/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1818 the settlement was renamed Fredericktown after Colonel Frederick, honoring his legacy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.achp.gov/preserve-america/community/fredericktown-missouri",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1899 Madison County Courthouse, designed by Theodore Link, now graces the historic downtown and is listed on the National Register.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.fredericktownmo.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A historic train depot, converted into a popular restaurant, showcases Fredericktown’s railroad heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.fredericktownmo.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Fredericktown’s roots lie in lead mining, with French explorers first seeking silver in the area during the early 1700s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
